#lang r7rs
;; r7rs-lang-plan R1 / D8: `#e` on a non-integral literal would need an exact
;; rational, which `#lang r7rs` does not have until T2.  Reading `#e1.5` as
;; the inexact 1.5 would be a wrong answer wearing the exactness prefix, so
;; the reader refuses it and names the task that lifts the limit (T0 moved
;; the refusal into the one number parser, r7rs_numsyntax.inc).
;; A literal with a non-zero fractional part on purpose: `#e1.0` is integral
;; and reads fine as the exact 1.
(defn main [] : int
  (println #e1.5)
  0)
